#
# env.kv — the same heuristic, now firing on the storage-key pin in
# `app/src/repro.test.ts`. The scanner sees `SOMETHING_KEY: '<string>'` and
# calls it a secret-named assignment. These five are the localStorage key
# NAMES this app writes under: they are namespace strings, already exported as
# plain constants from `app/src/storageKeys.ts` and `engine/data/library.ts`,
# and visible to anyone who opens devtools on the page. They are not
# credentials and there is nothing to rotate.
#
# Written WITHOUT the surrounding quotes: the scanner's matched span starts
# after the opening quote (verified, col 27 on the CHAIN_STORAGE_KEY line), and
# only a finding whose matched text EQUALS an entry is suppressed. The first
# version of these five carried the quotes and suppressed nothing -- the push
# reported "11 entries suppressed 0 finding(s)", which is what an allowlist
# that matches nothing looks like.
#
# They are in a test on purpose and must stay there. Replacing these literals
# with the constants is exactly what broke the pin: a test that reads the
# constant it claims to pin cannot fail when the constant changes. Measured
# before the fix: renaming every key while keeping the `brio.` prefix passed
# all 333 tests and would silently orphan every saved track, inventory and
# hand-measured submission on every existing install.
brio.chain.v0
